---
// How one request moves through OpenPike. Plain SVG, colored by CSS custom properties so it
// follows the light and dark themes. No inline styles, so the docs CSP needs nothing for it.
---

<svg class="op-flow" viewBox="0 0 790 236" role="img" aria-labelledby="op-flow-title op-flow-desc">
  <title id="op-flow-title">How a request flows through OpenPike</title>
  <desc id="op-flow-desc">
    Your agent or app sends a request with an OpenPike virtual key to api.openpike.dev. OpenPike checks the key, then budgets, pauses,
    loop limits and plan limits, and forwards the request with your own provider key. The response streams straight back, and the
    usage and cost are recorded after it ends.
  </desc>
  <defs>
    <marker id="op-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="op-flow-arrowhead"></path>
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <rect x="8" y="70" width="150" height="72" rx="10" class="op-flow-box"></rect>
  <text x="83" y="100" class="op-flow-title">Your agent or app</text>
  <text x="83" y="122" class="op-flow-note">opk_live_...</text>

  <rect x="230" y="20" width="330" height="196" rx="12" class="op-flow-box op-flow-gateway"></rect>
  <text x="395" y="48" class="op-flow-title">api.openpike.dev</text>
  <text x="252" y="82" class="op-flow-step">1. Check the virtual key</text>
  <text x="252" y="110" class="op-flow-step">2. Budgets, pauses, loop limits</text>
  <text x="252" y="138" class="op-flow-step">3. Plan limits</text>
  <text x="252" y="166" class="op-flow-step">4. Pick the model and your provider key</text>
  <text x="252" y="194" class="op-flow-step">5. Record tokens and cost after the response</text>

  <rect x="632" y="70" width="150" height="72" rx="10" class="op-flow-box"></rect>
  <text x="707" y="100" class="op-flow-title">Provider</text>
  <text x="707" y="122" class="op-flow-note">with your own key</text>

  <line x1="160" y1="96" x2="226" y2="96" class="op-flow-line" marker-end="url(#op-arrow)"></line>
  <line x1="564" y1="96" x2="628" y2="96" class="op-flow-line" marker-end="url(#op-arrow)"></line>
  <line x1="628" y1="120" x2="564" y2="120" class="op-flow-line op-flow-back" marker-end="url(#op-arrow)"></line>
  <line x1="226" y1="120" x2="160" y2="120" class="op-flow-line op-flow-back" marker-end="url(#op-arrow)"></line>
  <text x="596" y="140" class="op-flow-note">stream</text>
  <text x="193" y="140" class="op-flow-note">stream</text>
</svg>
